oom with them, they cannot fast.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrBut the days will come, when the bridegroom shall be taken away from them, and then shall they fast in those days.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book(§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ•No man also seweth a piece of new cloth on an old garment: else the new piece that filled it up taketh away from the old, and the rent is made worse.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ»And no man putteth new wine into old bottles: else the new wine doth burst the bottles, and the wine is spilled, and the bottles will be marred: but new wine must be put into new bottles.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book(§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd it came to pass, that he went through the corn fields on the sabbath day; and his disciples began, as they went, to pluck the ears of corn.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙaAnd the Pharisees said unto him, Behold, why do they on the sabbath day that which is not lawful?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book(§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€And he said unto them, Have ye never read what David did, when he had need, and was an hungred, he, and they that were with him?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÀHow he went into the house of God in the days of Abiathar the high priest, and did eat the shewbread, which is not lawful to eat but for the priests, and gave also to them which were with him?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book(§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙQAnd he said unto them, The sabbath was made for man, and not man for the sabbath:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ5therefore the Son of man is Lord also of the sabbath.¦layout ªlast_verse